. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H4 * 
. 
.         * Model description: We calculate two OLS regressions separately for 
> male respondents and female respondents regressing
.         * gender equality attitudes as measured in 2018 on having a daughter 
> rather than a son as first child with some
.         * sociodemographic controls and an indicator on months passed since b
> irth of first child. Based on these two regressions,
.         * we estimate the difference in the daughter effect for male and fema
> le respondents simultaneously (using the suest 
.         * command) and calculate a Wald X2 test for equality of daughter coef
> ficients of male and female respondents to test for 
.         * statistical significance of the difference.
. 
.         reg equal_wc_2018_1 ib0.daughter if gender==0   // only fathers 

      Source |       SS           df       MS      Number of obs   =         8
-------------+----------------------------------   F(1, 6)         =      1.55
       Model |       6.125         1       6.125   Prob > F        =    0.2599
    Residual |       23.75         6  3.95833333   R-squared       =    0.2050
-------------+----------------------------------   Adj R-squared   =    0.0725
       Total |      29.875         7  4.26785714   Root MSE        =    1.9896

